1
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,880
I'm the mother of Mina,
the employee you assaulted.

2
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:17,919
<i>Why did you call an executive meeting?</i>

3
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:21,239
<i>I just wanted you and Claire
to prove yourselves.</i>

4
00:00:21,240 --> 00:00:23,039
Did you really think we were friends?

5
00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:25,119
<i>You hired the two of us to be your friends</i>

6
00:00:25,120 --> 00:00:28,119
<i>so you'd look more popular
than other socialites.</i>

7
00:00:28,120 --> 00:00:30,159
<i>If Claire had proof I cheated on you,</i>

8
00:00:30,160 --> 00:00:32,199
<i>she would've used it by now!</i>

9
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:34,719
He won't suspect anything
about my shellfish allergy?

10
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:38,080
<i>But if you found out Claire was
hiding something from you,</i>

11
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:39,520
what would you say?

12
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:45,840
What is it, Claire?

13
00:00:46,920 --> 00:00:49,040
- Mom.
- Let me tell him.

14
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:53,320
So your dad can wake up
and see things for what they are.

15
00:00:55,040 --> 00:00:58,759
I overheard Claire and Chan

16
00:00:58,760 --> 00:01:02,320
talk about
her shellfish allergy being a lie.

17
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:14,760
<i>About me being in your room...</i>

18
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:17,760
He won't suspect anything
about my shellfish allergy?

19
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:21,720
I won't tell anyone.

20
00:01:26,640 --> 00:01:30,720
Uh, but I really am allergic to shellfish.

21
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:37,920
Then why did you say that?

22
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:46,840
What are you two hiding from him?

23
00:01:49,840 --> 00:01:51,080
What's going on, Claire?

24
00:01:57,920 --> 00:01:59,000
Well...

25
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:03,800
Claire.

26
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:08,720
I think it's time you told him the truth.

27
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:18,360
Is there something
you want to tell me, Claire?

28
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:23,720
About...

29
00:02:36,160 --> 00:02:38,520
Claire said she wanted to go back to work.

30
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:42,240
Really?

31
00:02:43,880 --> 00:02:45,280
Yes, sir.

32
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:53,200
I think Ms. Rin only caught
a part of my conversation with Claire.

33
00:02:53,960 --> 00:02:56,439
Claire told me
she wanted to go back to work,

34
00:02:56,440 --> 00:03:01,080
but she was worried you would wonder
how she recovered so fast.

35
00:03:01,960 --> 00:03:05,440
She was worried you would think
she faked the allergy.

36
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:12,960
I thought you might want to
take it easy for a while longer.

37
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:15,519
I thought so too at first, sir.

38
00:03:15,520 --> 00:03:18,480
But Claire said
she wants to go back to work.

39
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:21,319
She wanted to get her brain active again.

40
00:03:21,320 --> 00:03:23,080
So I was thinking,

41
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:25,960
if she uses her brain more often,

42
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:29,440
she might get her memory back faster.

43
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:40,439
That's a good idea.

44
00:03:40,440 --> 00:03:41,720
I think that's a good idea.

45
00:03:43,320 --> 00:03:46,480
Because I've been meaning
to give you something.

46
00:03:54,960 --> 00:03:55,880
Well?

47
00:03:56,720 --> 00:03:58,240
Does anyone have any questions?

48
00:05:34,840 --> 00:05:38,479
Are you crazy?
You want me to go back to work?

49
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:40,439
You're the crazy one.

50
00:05:40,440 --> 00:05:43,599
Why didn't you tell me
Ms. Rossarin snuck in here?

51
00:05:43,600 --> 00:05:44,959
Hey, is something wrong?

52
00:05:44,960 --> 00:05:47,840
The floor was slippery, so I got startled.

53
00:05:49,200 --> 00:05:50,200
It's really nothing.

54
00:05:54,320 --> 00:05:55,320
Well...

55
00:05:56,640 --> 00:05:58,959
I just didn't want to make a scene.

56
00:05:58,960 --> 00:06:01,759
If I told you, you'd tell Grandpa.

57
00:06:01,760 --> 00:06:03,239
Then he'd chew out Aunt Rin.

58
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:04,640
There'd be a big fight.

59
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:06,840
I looked out for him.

60
00:06:10,120 --> 00:06:11,159
Alright.

61
00:06:11,160 --> 00:06:12,439
Then,

62
00:06:12,440 --> 00:06:17,279
you need to memorize TGL's business
profile and entire structure tonight.

63
00:06:17,280 --> 00:06:18,200
Huh?

64
00:06:19,160 --> 00:06:20,519
Do I really have to go to work?

65
00:06:20,520 --> 00:06:21,879
Yes.

66
00:06:21,880 --> 00:06:24,999
And you're about to ask me
why you even have to, right?

67
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:29,679
It's because you made
Ms. Rossarin and Ms. Cha suspicious.

68
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:31,759
And right now, those two

69
00:06:31,760 --> 00:06:35,520
are using your amnesia
to paint you as weak to get rid of you.

70
00:06:36,400 --> 00:06:39,160
The only way to solve this problem is

71
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:42,319
you have to show everyone that

72
00:06:42,320 --> 00:06:44,600
you're the same old Claire.

73
00:06:50,400 --> 00:06:52,080
But I don't know what I'm doing.

74
00:06:59,640 --> 00:07:01,040
You can do it.

75
00:07:02,400 --> 00:07:03,680
Trust me.

76
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:23,960
Hey.

77
00:07:25,560 --> 00:07:27,160
You can go to bed first.

78
00:07:27,880 --> 00:07:30,400
No need to watch me.
You didn't sleep last night either.

79
00:07:47,520 --> 00:07:51,480
And here I thought he was a robot.
So he crashes like the rest of us.

80
00:08:25,040 --> 00:08:26,840
I know you're a good person deep down.

81
00:08:30,160 --> 00:08:33,440
Is it so hard for you
to smile once in a while?

82
00:08:44,400 --> 00:08:45,720
Better not.

83
00:08:46,400 --> 00:08:48,480
He'll wake up
and accuse me of something again.

84
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:10,320
EMPLOYMENT AGREEMENT
BETWEEN CLAIRE AND YO & PATCHY

85
00:10:09,880 --> 00:10:11,160
Hey.

86
00:10:12,720 --> 00:10:15,640
Why didn't you tell me
you were coming out here?

87
00:10:16,240 --> 00:10:19,160
Well, you were fast asleep.
I didn't want to wake you.

88
00:10:19,960 --> 00:10:21,959
Besides, it's not like I left.

89
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:24,600
I just came out to get some fresh air.

90
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:31,440
Let me ask you something.

91
00:10:32,760 --> 00:10:35,039
Aside from Ms. Yo and Ms. Patchy,

92
00:10:35,040 --> 00:10:37,920
her other celeb friends I saw on TV...

93
00:10:38,560 --> 00:10:42,120
were they all hired to be
Ms. Claire's friends too?

94
00:10:48,720 --> 00:10:49,800
Yes.

95
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:55,080
Everyone had a different agenda.

96
00:10:55,720 --> 00:11:00,560
It all depended on what kind of image
Claire wanted to pull off at the time.

97
00:11:01,160 --> 00:11:02,440
Seriously?

98
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:14,000
Did you know that
we only see one side of the moon?

99
00:11:14,880 --> 00:11:15,960
No.

100
00:11:16,680 --> 00:11:18,520
I never really noticed.

101
00:11:21,080 --> 00:11:24,640
Looking up from Earth, we only
see the side with the rabbit on it.

102
00:11:27,120 --> 00:11:28,120
Why is that?

103
00:11:28,720 --> 00:11:31,520
Maybe that's all the moon wants us to see.

104
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:38,600
But actually, the moon has a dark side

105
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:40,760
where sunlight never reaches.

106
00:11:41,800 --> 00:11:46,600
So we never see it and we assume
the moon has only one side.

107
00:11:53,560 --> 00:11:54,480
You're right.

108
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:58,560
I've never noticed that
until you mentioned it.

109
00:12:00,680 --> 00:12:02,520
People are just like the moon.

110
00:12:03,200 --> 00:12:07,000
We always choose to show
our good and beautiful side.

111
00:12:07,800 --> 00:12:11,040
When in reality,
whether it's the moon or people,

112
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:13,400
there are always two sides.

113
00:12:13,920 --> 00:12:18,599
Even with people
you think you know inside out,

114
00:12:18,600 --> 00:12:22,119
there might be
a side to them you've never seen.

115
00:12:22,120 --> 00:12:26,480
Or maybe they're hiding it
because they don't want you to see it.

116
00:12:27,400 --> 00:12:28,880
Like Ms. Claire, right?

117
00:12:30,360 --> 00:12:35,760
I guess this is a side of her
I never knew existed.

118
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:40,920
But did she really never have any friends?

119
00:12:44,640 --> 00:12:49,000
That depends on how
you define the word "friend."

120
00:12:50,160 --> 00:12:52,199
Claire chose not to have friends

121
00:12:52,200 --> 00:12:54,920
because she didn't need them.

122
00:12:56,440 --> 00:13:01,600
You make it sound like
she had issues in the friend department.

123
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:07,720
I'm just trying to explain
what it's like for rich people.

124
00:13:08,600 --> 00:13:10,679
Rich people hang out for mutual benefits.

125
00:13:10,680 --> 00:13:14,480
That's why the word "friend"
doesn't really apply.

126
00:13:34,200 --> 00:13:35,160
Aunt.

127
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:40,720
Don't leave me to become
a star up there just yet.

128
00:13:42,480 --> 00:13:43,400
I'm fighting.

129
00:13:44,160 --> 00:13:45,720
You have to fight too.

130
00:14:17,720 --> 00:14:19,640
I can do this.

131
00:14:35,520 --> 00:14:36,440
You're still here?

132
00:14:39,080 --> 00:14:41,999
I figured you'd be rolling out
the red carpet at the office

133
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:43,800
to welcome Claire back to work.

134
00:14:44,920 --> 00:14:45,879
Tell me the truth,

135
00:14:45,880 --> 00:14:50,480
did she really want to go back to work,
or did you make her?

136
00:14:52,640 --> 00:14:54,040
What makes you ask that?

137
00:14:54,640 --> 00:14:55,799
I don't know.

138
00:14:55,800 --> 00:14:59,200
Ever since Claire got back,
you've been calling all the shots.

139
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:03,720
I'm starting to wonder
if she's the real Claire or an impostor.

140
00:15:10,440 --> 00:15:12,240
Ms. Cha, you might be forgetting

141
00:15:12,880 --> 00:15:15,599
that she hasn't fully
recovered her memory.

142
00:15:15,600 --> 00:15:19,240
So it's my job
to guide her through everything.

143
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:23,360
But if you want to take over,
I'm happy to step aside.

144
00:15:26,560 --> 00:15:30,280
I'd really love to know
what you and Claire are plotting.

145
00:15:35,960 --> 00:15:37,720
Is Claire still upstairs?

146
00:15:39,720 --> 00:15:40,600
Yes, sir.

147
00:15:41,720 --> 00:15:44,120
Her stylist is
putting on the finishing touches.

148
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:47,240
I'm off to work.

149
00:15:57,160 --> 00:15:59,000
Things have been hard for you.

150
00:16:00,600 --> 00:16:02,000
It's my job, sir.

151
00:16:02,600 --> 00:16:03,520
I know.

152
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:08,760
But if a board meeting is called
to do what they did yesterday,

153
00:16:09,360 --> 00:16:10,920
I need to be informed!

154
00:16:12,480 --> 00:16:14,720
That little thing
wouldn't affect my heart.

155
00:16:31,400 --> 00:16:32,840
What are those looks?

156
00:16:36,880 --> 00:16:38,040
How do I look?

157
00:16:43,840 --> 00:16:47,120
At first, I was worried
you weren't ready to go back to work.

158
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:51,239
But seeing you like this,

159
00:16:51,240 --> 00:16:52,920
I think you're ready.

160
00:16:54,560 --> 00:16:55,960
Have a good day at work.

161
00:16:56,520 --> 00:16:58,920
And if you're unsure about anything,
just ask Chan.

162
00:16:59,920 --> 00:17:02,159
With him there,
you have nothing to worry about.

163
00:17:02,160 --> 00:17:07,400
But if anyone picks on you
or says anything out of line, you tell me.

164
00:17:10,079 --> 00:17:13,119
You sound like you're dropping me off
on my first day of preschool.

165
00:17:16,520 --> 00:17:17,639
Go on.

166
00:17:17,640 --> 00:17:18,920
Chan.

167
00:17:20,359 --> 00:17:21,400
Keep an eye on her.

168
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:22,839
I will.

169
00:17:24,640 --> 00:17:25,800
I'm off.

170
00:17:36,520 --> 00:17:37,560
He seems to be in a great mood today.

171
00:17:52,320 --> 00:17:53,800
Thank you.

172
00:17:59,680 --> 00:18:03,200
You probably reminded him of
when he used to drop you off at preschool.

173
00:18:06,680 --> 00:18:09,680
He reminded me of my aunt
dropping me off back then too.

174
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:17,640
Even though I know miracles are rare,

175
00:18:18,440 --> 00:18:21,880
I still hope one day my aunt
will go back to the way she was.

176
00:18:38,840 --> 00:18:41,360
Can we make a quick stop on the way?

177
00:18:42,880 --> 00:18:43,720
Where?

178
00:18:47,120 --> 00:18:48,840
YUWADEE PANICH

179
00:18:50,760 --> 00:18:51,879
I'll get money at home.

180
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:52,799
Hey, the car...

181
00:18:52,800 --> 00:18:54,559
It's five baht.

182
00:18:54,560 --> 00:18:56,839
- I'll be back.
- You two can wait here.

183
00:18:56,840 --> 00:18:57,960
I'll be right back.

184
00:18:58,880 --> 00:18:59,880
I'm coming with you.

185
00:19:01,400 --> 00:19:02,919
What, afraid I'll run away?

186
00:19:02,920 --> 00:19:05,679
I'm just grabbing something.
I'll be in and out.

187
00:19:05,680 --> 00:19:07,160
Tun, I'll be right back.

188
00:19:09,080 --> 00:19:11,440
I think it's best if he goes with you.

189
00:19:13,240 --> 00:19:15,000
You're just as bad as him.

190
00:19:17,600 --> 00:19:19,640
Let me know if you need anything.

191
00:19:24,520 --> 00:19:26,320
Hey, I'll come get it later.

192
00:19:56,920 --> 00:19:57,840
Go on in.

193
00:20:34,640 --> 00:20:37,080
I thought you said
you had no other relatives.

194
00:20:38,440 --> 00:20:39,640
Then who did this?

195
00:20:42,760 --> 00:20:43,720
I don't know.

196
00:20:44,760 --> 00:20:47,160
Maybe the neighbors.

197
00:20:51,240 --> 00:20:55,240
Well, let's grab what you need
and get out of here.

198
00:21:06,480 --> 00:21:07,720
This is all I came for.

199
00:21:21,600 --> 00:21:22,480
Wait.

200
00:21:23,360 --> 00:21:24,320
That's...

201
00:21:44,520 --> 00:21:45,680
Hey.

202
00:21:46,520 --> 00:21:48,680
Can I stay a little longer?

203
00:22:43,680 --> 00:22:44,520
Aunt Lin.

204
00:22:45,440 --> 00:22:46,280
Jin.

205
00:22:47,320 --> 00:22:48,240
It's me.

206
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:54,120
Give me a second.

207
00:23:32,480 --> 00:23:33,320
Much better.

208
00:23:36,640 --> 00:23:37,480
Wan.

209
00:23:38,560 --> 00:23:39,800
Jin.

210
00:23:40,480 --> 00:23:42,520
Do you know why I came today?

211
00:23:46,400 --> 00:23:47,759
Look!

212
00:23:47,760 --> 00:23:49,640
I brought you the award.

213
00:23:50,400 --> 00:23:53,360
You remember what this is, right?

214
00:23:58,040 --> 00:23:59,080
Tada!

215
00:24:01,400 --> 00:24:02,760
What is this?

216
00:24:03,960 --> 00:24:08,839
The Idol Award for
Best Content of the Year goes to...

217
00:24:08,840 --> 00:24:13,280
Ms. Jinla Phiandaidee!

218
00:24:14,280 --> 00:24:15,120
Here.

219
00:24:15,720 --> 00:24:16,799
I had it made for you.

220
00:24:16,800 --> 00:24:20,759
To cheer up my best friend.

221
00:24:20,760 --> 00:24:21,800
Hey.

222
00:24:24,600 --> 00:24:28,239
It's okay, girl. Don't cry. Don't be sad.

223
00:24:28,240 --> 00:24:30,359
You can always win next year.

224
00:24:30,360 --> 00:24:32,919
Stop, stop. Who said I even wanted it?

225
00:24:32,920 --> 00:24:36,319
Hey, I worked so hard on this.
You don't want it?

226
00:24:36,320 --> 00:24:38,880
Don't you want to win anything
once in your career?

227
00:24:40,680 --> 00:24:41,840
No.

228
00:24:42,400 --> 00:24:43,479
Think about it.

229
00:24:43,480 --> 00:24:45,999
The job is stressful enough.

230
00:24:46,000 --> 00:24:48,639
If you're doing your job to win an award,

231
00:24:48,640 --> 00:24:50,640
that's double the stress.

232
00:24:54,400 --> 00:24:55,639
Hey.

233
00:24:55,640 --> 00:24:58,119
You don't need to comfort me.

234
00:24:58,120 --> 00:25:02,240
I get an award every single second
of every single day anyway.

235
00:25:03,760 --> 00:25:05,159
What are you on about?

236
00:25:05,160 --> 00:25:07,160
Duh, all of this.

237
00:25:11,960 --> 00:25:14,119
Just being alive

238
00:25:14,120 --> 00:25:16,080
and enjoying life.

239
00:25:16,800 --> 00:25:18,760
That's the best award there is.

240
00:25:22,760 --> 00:25:24,800
Spoken like a true idealist.

241
00:25:27,160 --> 00:25:29,680
So you don't want it.

242
00:25:30,320 --> 00:25:31,759
Fine, I'm taking it back.

243
00:25:31,760 --> 00:25:33,040
Oh, wait, wait.

244
00:25:35,480 --> 00:25:36,840
You had it made, so give it.

245
00:25:38,400 --> 00:25:40,799
I knew you wouldn't turn me down.

246
00:25:40,800 --> 00:25:41,920
Let's do it again.

247
00:25:44,120 --> 00:25:49,559
The Idol Award for
Best Content of the Year

248
00:25:49,560 --> 00:25:51,439
goes to...

249
00:25:51,440 --> 00:25:54,359
Ms. Jinla Phiandaidee!

250
00:25:54,360 --> 00:25:57,359
Let's hear it for her.
Thank you very much.

251
00:25:57,360 --> 00:25:59,639
Can I get a round of applause?

252
00:25:59,640 --> 00:26:03,479
I can't believe this is happening.
Is this for real? Thank you. For real?

253
00:26:03,480 --> 00:26:04,839
It's all yours.

254
00:26:04,840 --> 00:26:06,440
Thank you.

255
00:26:30,560 --> 00:26:35,640
Okay, now that you're in heaven, you might
have forgotten what this award was about.

256
00:26:37,040 --> 00:26:40,240
It's the one we used to
joke around with, remember?

257
00:26:41,440 --> 00:26:42,520
But right now,

258
00:26:43,680 --> 00:26:45,320
it really is yours, Jin.

259
00:26:47,440 --> 00:26:49,480
You actually won for real.

260
00:26:53,520 --> 00:26:55,320
I'm so happy for you.

261
00:26:58,800 --> 00:27:00,320
Your article...

262
00:27:01,480 --> 00:27:02,640
won.

263
00:27:04,600 --> 00:27:07,720
I always knew my bestie was the greatest.

264
00:27:08,480 --> 00:27:11,240
Nobody deserves this more than you.

265
00:27:15,880 --> 00:27:16,720
Here.

266
00:27:27,440 --> 00:27:28,520
Wan.

267
00:27:39,880 --> 00:27:40,760
Who's there?

268
00:27:51,200 --> 00:27:52,880
I asked who's there.

269
00:28:12,160 --> 00:28:13,600
This is the house.

270
00:28:14,640 --> 00:28:18,719
You two go check it out
and send photos to those guys.

271
00:28:18,720 --> 00:28:20,279
When are they getting here?

272
00:28:20,280 --> 00:28:23,719
And see what we can sell
and separate those items.

273
00:28:23,720 --> 00:28:24,919
Move it.

274
00:28:24,920 --> 00:28:25,840
Let's go.

275
00:28:31,680 --> 00:28:34,519
What are you guys doing here?

276
00:28:34,520 --> 00:28:35,600
Who are you?

277
00:28:36,720 --> 00:28:38,040
I'm Jin's friend.

278
00:28:40,920 --> 00:28:42,240
Is there another way out?

279
00:28:43,760 --> 00:28:45,080
Yes. In the back.

280
00:28:50,080 --> 00:28:51,000
Jin's friend.

281
00:28:52,200 --> 00:28:53,320
Nice to meet you.

282
00:28:56,560 --> 00:28:58,080
I'm your friend's creditor.

283
00:28:59,920 --> 00:29:00,879
What?

284
00:29:00,880 --> 00:29:03,360
Didn't you know she took a loan from me?

285
00:29:05,480 --> 00:29:07,960
But you do know Jin passed away, right?

286
00:29:09,640 --> 00:29:11,199
I hear they're both gone.

287
00:29:11,200 --> 00:29:14,120
Both Jin and her aunt.

288
00:29:14,720 --> 00:29:18,280
They're already dead.
What more do you want from them?

289
00:29:18,920 --> 00:29:20,279
True.

290
00:29:20,280 --> 00:29:22,280
Since I can't collect from Jin,

291
00:29:25,600 --> 00:29:27,040
can I collect from you?

292
00:29:30,600 --> 00:29:33,679
I'm sorry, I have to go to work.
Excuse me.

293
00:29:33,680 --> 00:29:34,840
What's the rush?

294
00:29:36,520 --> 00:29:39,239
She's been dead for a while,
yet you're still coming around.

295
00:29:39,240 --> 00:29:41,479
You two must've been real close.

296
00:29:41,480 --> 00:29:43,999
Maybe you should pay off her debt.

297
00:29:44,000 --> 00:29:47,279
Hey, let go of me.
I'm not playing around with you.

298
00:29:47,280 --> 00:29:48,359
I'm being nice here.

299
00:29:48,360 --> 00:29:50,399
Let me go, or I'm calling the police.

300
00:29:50,400 --> 00:29:52,199
Help! Somebody help!

301
00:29:52,200 --> 00:29:54,159
- Are you stupid or what?
- Get off me!

302
00:29:54,160 --> 00:29:55,240
You bitch.

303
00:30:09,240 --> 00:30:10,079
Move.

304
00:30:10,080 --> 00:30:13,680
It looks like
she doesn't want to talk to you.

305
00:30:14,640 --> 00:30:15,639
Oh, yeah?

306
00:30:15,640 --> 00:30:17,240
You think you're some kind of hero?

307
00:30:19,280 --> 00:30:22,599
Why does everyone assume
helping women is about being a hero?

308
00:30:22,600 --> 00:30:26,640
Isn't it just what
any decent guy should do?

309
00:30:29,160 --> 00:30:32,400
I think you guys should just leave.

310
00:30:34,120 --> 00:30:36,840
That's my line, asshole!

311
00:30:47,400 --> 00:30:48,520
Move.

312
00:30:51,360 --> 00:30:52,560
I gave you a warning.

313
00:30:53,640 --> 00:30:55,560
Hey, let's get him!

314
00:31:26,600 --> 00:31:29,280
- Hey, get up.
- Well done.

315
00:31:32,320 --> 00:31:34,440
Don't let me see you around here again!

316
00:31:40,400 --> 00:31:41,960
Tough guys, where are you going?!

317
00:31:42,560 --> 00:31:45,359
If you're so tough,
stop picking on women, assholes!

318
00:31:45,360 --> 00:31:46,720
You think I'm scared?

319
00:32:04,320 --> 00:32:06,000
Are you...

320
00:32:06,600 --> 00:32:07,920
Are you okay?

321
00:32:10,280 --> 00:32:12,640
I'm fine. I'm totally fine.

322
00:32:13,240 --> 00:32:17,560
I'm so sorry
for dragging you into that mess.

323
00:32:18,840 --> 00:32:19,999
Don't worry about it.

324
00:32:20,000 --> 00:32:23,720
Like I said,
it's what any decent guy should do.

325
00:32:26,520 --> 00:32:28,800
Were they going to sell
your friend's belongings?

326
00:32:29,400 --> 00:32:34,240
Yes. She owed them money. They were
probably trying to get their money back.

327
00:32:35,040 --> 00:32:37,160
What about you? You live around here?

328
00:32:39,840 --> 00:32:40,840
Hold on a second.

329
00:32:42,920 --> 00:32:43,760
Hello?

330
00:32:45,280 --> 00:32:46,120
Yeah.

331
00:32:46,840 --> 00:32:49,239
I stepped out to take care of something.

332
00:32:49,240 --> 00:32:51,440
I'm on my way. Okay.

333
00:32:53,840 --> 00:32:55,000
I have to run.

334
00:32:55,600 --> 00:32:57,199
Oh, okay.

335
00:32:57,200 --> 00:33:00,400
Thank you so much
for saving me back there.

336
00:33:01,560 --> 00:33:02,520
You're welcome.

337
00:33:03,960 --> 00:33:06,800
She was lucky to have
a great friend like you, Ms. Wan.

338
00:33:08,400 --> 00:33:09,320
I have to go.

339
00:33:28,640 --> 00:33:31,400
I was so flustered
I forgot to get his name.

340
00:33:34,600 --> 00:33:35,520
Wait...

341
00:33:36,680 --> 00:33:38,320
How did he know my name?

342
00:33:47,440 --> 00:33:49,240
Hello, Ball?

343
00:33:50,600 --> 00:33:51,960
Did you need something?

344
00:33:55,960 --> 00:33:56,840
What?

345
00:33:57,800 --> 00:33:59,960
Socialite Claire's back in the news?

346
00:34:07,920 --> 00:34:09,880
Tun's on his way. Let's wait in the car.

347
00:34:18,040 --> 00:34:19,080
You know,

348
00:34:20,000 --> 00:34:21,480
being in my house just now

349
00:34:22,880 --> 00:34:26,120
was the best I've felt since I woke up.

350
00:34:28,639 --> 00:34:30,039
It's weird.

351
00:34:30,040 --> 00:34:32,839
Right now, I'm Ms. Claire,
who has everything.

352
00:34:32,840 --> 00:34:34,799
Living in a mansion.

353
00:34:34,800 --> 00:34:36,919
Having people wait on me.

354
00:34:36,920 --> 00:34:38,600
Getting whatever I want.

355
00:34:39,840 --> 00:34:42,560
But I've never been as happy
as I was when I saw Wan.

356
00:34:52,880 --> 00:34:54,040
Hey...

357
00:34:56,280 --> 00:34:57,560
Why are you smiling?

358
00:35:00,240 --> 00:35:02,759
I just saw an upside to being poor.

359
00:35:02,760 --> 00:35:06,119
You don't have to worry
whether the friends you make

360
00:35:06,120 --> 00:35:08,640
are only around for money or benefits.

361
00:35:18,640 --> 00:35:19,680
What's up?

362
00:35:20,280 --> 00:35:21,120
What?

363
00:35:24,720 --> 00:35:26,040
I'll be right there.

364
00:35:27,040 --> 00:35:28,200
What's going on?

365
00:35:29,640 --> 00:35:32,800
Someone leaked that Claire hired
Yo and Patchy to be her friends.

366
00:35:49,640 --> 00:35:51,639
The press is swarming the office.

367
00:35:51,640 --> 00:35:54,240
I don't think she should go in today.

368
00:35:57,080 --> 00:35:58,120
What do you think?

369
00:36:03,320 --> 00:36:07,120
If you ask me, I agree with Mr. Tun.

370
00:36:08,880 --> 00:36:10,719
But if it were Ms. Claire,

371
00:36:10,720 --> 00:36:15,560
she would strut right in with her head
held high, acting like nothing happened.

372
00:36:28,400 --> 00:36:29,559
Hello?

373
00:36:29,560 --> 00:36:30,800
Ms. Patchy.

374
00:36:32,280 --> 00:36:33,799
I saw the news.

375
00:36:33,800 --> 00:36:34,720
<i>And?</i>

376
00:36:35,600 --> 00:36:38,480
You don't sound very worried.

377
00:36:39,080 --> 00:36:42,199
It definitely didn't leak from my side.

378
00:36:42,200 --> 00:36:43,199
<i>Really?</i>

379
00:36:43,200 --> 00:36:46,440
- Are you pointing fingers at us then?
- <i>Hold on.</i>

380
00:36:47,080 --> 00:36:49,760
Let's not start playing
the blame game right now.

381
00:36:50,520 --> 00:36:53,519
I need both of you
to deny the story for now

382
00:36:53,520 --> 00:36:57,160
<i>and confirm publicly that
you and Claire are genuine friends.</i>

383
00:36:57,760 --> 00:36:59,560
I'll handle the rest.

384
00:37:00,280 --> 00:37:01,240
That's all.

385
00:37:03,920 --> 00:37:04,920
Hey.

386
00:37:05,840 --> 00:37:08,320
What if those two leaked it themselves

387
00:37:09,000 --> 00:37:11,400
just to extort more money from you?

388
00:37:13,640 --> 00:37:14,640
No way.

389
00:37:15,400 --> 00:37:18,400
They know better than
to try and blackmail Claire.

390
00:37:22,280 --> 00:37:24,280
Then how do you think it got out?

391
00:37:29,080 --> 00:37:31,000
There's only one person it could be.

392
00:37:47,440 --> 00:37:49,639
Why are we at the office, Cha?

393
00:37:49,640 --> 00:37:51,880
Don't we have a meeting with Ms. Mon?

394
00:37:53,120 --> 00:37:54,800
I pushed it to next week.

395
00:37:55,680 --> 00:37:59,000
Today, I'd rather be here
to watch the drama unfold.

396
00:38:10,680 --> 00:38:13,879
Oh, Ms. Cha!
Can we get a quick statement, Ms. Cha?

397
00:38:13,880 --> 00:38:18,480
Ms. Cha, did you know about Ms. Claire
paying celebrities to be her friends?

398
00:38:19,720 --> 00:38:23,799
Even though we're family,
we don't share everything.

399
00:38:23,800 --> 00:38:26,679
As for Claire
hiring celebrities to be her friends,

400
00:38:26,680 --> 00:38:29,359
I just found out from the news myself.

401
00:38:29,360 --> 00:38:31,399
You'll have to ask Claire herself.

402
00:38:31,400 --> 00:38:34,079
Does that mean she's coming in today?

403
00:38:34,080 --> 00:38:35,480
That's what I heard.

404
00:38:36,000 --> 00:38:38,079
Whoa, is she really coming?

405
00:38:38,080 --> 00:38:39,239
Excuse me.

406
00:38:39,240 --> 00:38:41,880
Thank you, Ms. Cha. Thank you.

407
00:38:42,960 --> 00:38:43,800
Is Ms. Claire coming?

408
00:38:47,520 --> 00:38:49,600
Cha, is this true about Claire?

409
00:38:50,360 --> 00:38:51,679
Which part?

410
00:38:51,680 --> 00:38:55,800
The part about hiring celeb friends,
or the part about her coming in today?

411
00:38:56,440 --> 00:38:59,600
But it looks like you're
more curious about her return.

412
00:39:00,840 --> 00:39:02,119
Cha.

413
00:39:02,120 --> 00:39:04,679
If the rumors are true,

414
00:39:04,680 --> 00:39:07,920
it could damage
the company's image and credibility.

415
00:39:09,560 --> 00:39:12,239
Maybe I should give you a raise.

416
00:39:12,240 --> 00:39:16,720
Because on top of being an architect,
you're worried about our image.

417
00:39:18,080 --> 00:39:20,880
But before you worry about our image,

418
00:39:25,520 --> 00:39:27,440
maybe worry about yourself first.

419
00:39:28,040 --> 00:39:30,320
Because you're being too obvious.

420
00:39:35,320 --> 00:39:36,680
Get to work.

421
00:39:51,120 --> 00:39:52,680
Are you ready to be Claire?

422
00:40:14,840 --> 00:40:16,639
Whoa! Ms. Claire is really here!

423
00:40:16,640 --> 00:40:18,919
Ms. Claire, can we get a statement?

424
00:40:18,920 --> 00:40:20,920
Ms. Claire, this way, please.

425
00:40:27,040 --> 00:40:28,200
Hey, she's coming.

426
00:40:30,240 --> 00:40:32,919
Is it true you paid Ms. Patchy,

427
00:40:32,920 --> 00:40:35,800
Ms. Yo, and other celebs
to pose as your friends?

428
00:40:36,640 --> 00:40:38,640
Is it true?

429
00:40:40,920 --> 00:40:42,000
Of course not.

430
00:40:42,880 --> 00:40:44,440
Why would she do that?

431
00:40:45,200 --> 00:40:46,319
Right?

432
00:40:46,320 --> 00:40:49,239
Um, but our sources claim

433
00:40:49,240 --> 00:40:52,399
Ms. Claire paid Ms. Patchy and Ms. Yo

434
00:40:52,400 --> 00:40:54,239
a hefty seven-figure sum.

435
00:40:54,240 --> 00:40:55,279
Is that true?

436
00:40:55,280 --> 00:40:56,679
- Yeah.
- Is it true?

437
00:40:56,680 --> 00:40:58,439
Seven figures?

438
00:40:58,440 --> 00:41:00,279
Is it true?

439
00:41:00,280 --> 00:41:02,479
- Is it true?
- Is it true?

440
00:41:02,480 --> 00:41:03,399
Is it true?

441
00:41:03,400 --> 00:41:05,279
- Please answer.
- Is it true?

442
00:41:05,280 --> 00:41:07,000
Ms. Claire, care to comment?

443
00:41:08,200 --> 00:41:10,399
Is it true?

444
00:41:10,400 --> 00:41:12,960
Ms. Claire, what's the truth?

445
00:41:13,520 --> 00:41:15,920
Ms. Claire, what's the truth?

446
00:41:16,520 --> 00:41:18,120
Then show me the proof.

447
00:41:19,640 --> 00:41:20,600
Well?

448
00:41:21,160 --> 00:41:22,400
Do you have any proof?

449
00:41:25,800 --> 00:41:28,240
If you don't, drop the story.

450
00:41:29,160 --> 00:41:32,279
Because if I team up with
Ms. Yo and Ms. Patchy in a lawsuit,

451
00:41:32,280 --> 00:41:33,840
you're gonna lose more than seven figures.

452
00:41:38,800 --> 00:41:42,119
Let me make this absolutely clear:

453
00:41:42,120 --> 00:41:44,720
I have never paid anyone to be my friend.

454
00:41:45,360 --> 00:41:46,639
Thank you.

455
00:41:46,640 --> 00:41:48,519
Got it. Thank you, Ms. Claire.

456
00:41:48,520 --> 00:41:49,440
Ms. Claire!

457
00:41:50,120 --> 00:41:51,199
You're a fraud!

458
00:41:51,200 --> 00:41:52,240
Claire.

459
00:41:55,000 --> 00:41:55,840
Hey!

460
00:41:56,720 --> 00:41:57,640
Wan?

461
00:41:59,240 --> 00:42:00,080
Hey.

462
00:42:01,680 --> 00:42:03,679
You spend money on your image,

463
00:42:03,680 --> 00:42:07,840
but when someone died because of you,
you don't take any responsibility!

464
00:42:10,880 --> 00:42:12,279
Everyone,

465
00:42:12,280 --> 00:42:15,720
I'm here to demand justice for my friend.

466
00:42:16,320 --> 00:42:19,080
Do you all remember the helicopter crash?

467
00:42:19,680 --> 00:42:22,560
Two people lost their lives
in that incident.

468
00:42:23,280 --> 00:42:24,640
One was the pilot.

469
00:42:25,200 --> 00:42:26,720
And the other was...

470
00:42:29,480 --> 00:42:31,320
The other was my friend.

471
00:42:33,480 --> 00:42:35,119
My friend is dead,

472
00:42:35,120 --> 00:42:38,360
and yet nobody is saying a word about it.

473
00:42:40,240 --> 00:42:41,320
What do you want?

474
00:42:42,160 --> 00:42:46,519
We can press charges against you
for assaulting Claire.

475
00:42:46,520 --> 00:42:47,959
Go right ahead.

476
00:42:47,960 --> 00:42:49,680
Get the cops to arrest me.

477
00:42:50,760 --> 00:42:52,360
But I will not be silenced.

478
00:42:53,000 --> 00:42:56,760
I will not be silenced
the way you silenced the truth about Jin.

479
00:43:00,920 --> 00:43:04,200
Ms. Claire, do you feel
even a shred of remorse

480
00:43:04,840 --> 00:43:07,120
for causing a person's death?

481
00:43:10,160 --> 00:43:13,560
Actually, make that two deaths.

482
00:43:16,320 --> 00:43:19,080
You destroyed my friend's family.

483
00:43:21,200 --> 00:43:24,840
Do you have any idea
how many people died because of you?

484
00:43:28,440 --> 00:43:30,520
- Let go.
- Hey.

485
00:43:31,120 --> 00:43:32,759
Everyone.

486
00:43:32,760 --> 00:43:36,160
These were my friend and her aunt.

487
00:43:38,600 --> 00:43:42,520
And both of them died
because of Ms. Claire.

488
00:43:45,600 --> 00:43:48,600
And she has never
taken responsibility for it.

489
00:44:12,600 --> 00:44:14,079
Hey, don't walk away!

490
00:44:14,080 --> 00:44:15,679
Come back and face it!

491
00:44:15,680 --> 00:44:17,639
Ms. Claire, you need to answer for this!

492
00:44:17,640 --> 00:44:18,800
Get off me!

493
00:44:19,520 --> 00:44:20,519
Ms. Claire!

494
00:44:20,520 --> 00:44:22,559
Keep taking photos! Get me on camera!

495
00:44:22,560 --> 00:44:26,759
And make sure to write these people
don't care about poor people's lives!

496
00:44:26,760 --> 00:44:27,959
Hey, that's enough.

497
00:44:27,960 --> 00:44:29,399
- Let go!
- That's enough.

498
00:44:29,400 --> 00:44:30,480
Stop taking photos.

499
00:44:31,120 --> 00:44:32,199
You?

500
00:44:32,200 --> 00:44:33,800
What are you doing here?

501
00:44:34,720 --> 00:44:37,159
I'm Ms. Claire's bodyguard.

502
00:44:37,160 --> 00:44:38,079
- So...
- Huh?!

503
00:44:38,080 --> 00:44:39,199
Come with me.

504
00:44:39,200 --> 00:44:40,879
No, let go of me!

505
00:44:40,880 --> 00:44:41,999
- Get off me!
- Wait!

506
00:44:42,000 --> 00:44:44,079
Ms. Claire, you need to answer for this!

507
00:44:44,080 --> 00:44:45,360
Please stop, guys.

508
00:44:48,720 --> 00:44:51,159
<i>Do you all remember the helicopter crash?</i>

509
00:44:51,160 --> 00:44:53,959
Two people lost their lives
in that incident.

510
00:44:53,960 --> 00:44:55,799
One was the pilot.

511
00:44:55,800 --> 00:44:57,800
<i>The other was my friend.</i>

512
00:44:59,680 --> 00:45:01,279
<i>I will not be silenced</i>

513
00:45:01,280 --> 00:45:03,959
the way you silenced the truth about Jin.

514
00:45:03,960 --> 00:45:06,639
Ms. Claire, do you feel
even a shred of remorse

515
00:45:06,640 --> 00:45:09,000
for causing a person's death?

516
00:45:18,480 --> 00:45:19,320
Tun.

517
00:45:22,680 --> 00:45:24,439
Keep her in that room.

518
00:45:24,440 --> 00:45:26,040
Don't let her leave.

519
00:45:27,400 --> 00:45:28,720
How's my friend?

520
00:45:30,480 --> 00:45:33,119
She ambushed you
and you're still worried about her?

521
00:45:33,120 --> 00:45:34,800
She didn't know it was me.

522
00:45:35,720 --> 00:45:37,280
What are you gonna do to her?

523
00:45:40,080 --> 00:45:41,680
I'll let the police handle it.

524
00:45:42,200 --> 00:45:44,600
Is that really necessary?

525
00:45:45,640 --> 00:45:48,920
Then what do I have to do
to make your friend drop this, huh?

526
00:45:50,000 --> 00:45:53,920
Do you realize how much damage
she just caused us?

527
00:45:54,560 --> 00:45:56,319
And if I do nothing,

528
00:45:56,320 --> 00:45:59,760
the public will think
you're dodging responsibility.

529
00:46:03,000 --> 00:46:03,920
Wait.

530
00:46:08,480 --> 00:46:10,000
Let me talk to her.

531
00:46:12,560 --> 00:46:14,519
You know Wan was that angry

532
00:46:14,520 --> 00:46:16,959
because she thought
Ms. Claire had caused my death

533
00:46:16,960 --> 00:46:19,000
and her people
didn't take any responsibility.

534
00:46:20,160 --> 00:46:22,200
I'm the only one
who can get through to her.

535
00:46:23,560 --> 00:46:24,880
Please.

536
00:46:27,960 --> 00:46:30,080
And who will you be when you talk to her?

537
00:46:30,880 --> 00:46:31,840
Jinla?

538
00:46:33,160 --> 00:46:34,360
Or Khaedarun?

539
00:46:39,400 --> 00:46:40,839
- Get in here.
- Let go of me.

540
00:46:40,840 --> 00:46:42,479
- Get in here.
- Let go!

541
00:46:42,480 --> 00:46:44,360
Sit down. Sit down!

542
00:46:52,960 --> 00:46:57,800
I never would've pegged you as her lapdog.

543
00:47:01,120 --> 00:47:02,960
And why are you putting me in here?

544
00:47:03,560 --> 00:47:06,039
Waiting for the cops to arrest me?

545
00:47:06,040 --> 00:47:07,240
I see.

546
00:47:07,880 --> 00:47:11,240
Maybe you're waiting for your
precious boss to come get her revenge.

547
00:47:11,960 --> 00:47:13,480
Is that why you're keeping me here?

548
00:47:14,560 --> 00:47:18,879
Ms. Claire would never do that.
But I need you to cool off.

549
00:47:18,880 --> 00:47:20,879
Cool off?

550
00:47:20,880 --> 00:47:24,600
If you want me to cool off,
get your boss here to talk to me.

551
00:47:26,080 --> 00:47:29,399
If you hadn't pulled that stunt,
I might've been able to.

552
00:47:29,400 --> 00:47:33,280
But after what you did,
I have to keep you away from her.

553
00:47:45,800 --> 00:47:47,120
Then move.

554
00:47:47,840 --> 00:47:48,920
I'm leaving.

555
00:47:49,960 --> 00:47:51,439
No, not yet.

556
00:47:51,440 --> 00:47:52,439
Hey!

557
00:47:52,440 --> 00:47:53,480
Ow, hey!

558
00:47:55,600 --> 00:47:56,440
Sit down.

559
00:47:58,240 --> 00:48:00,079
Are you okay?

560
00:48:00,080 --> 00:48:01,480
Leave me alone.

561
00:48:15,920 --> 00:48:17,280
Give us the room.

562
00:48:37,040 --> 00:48:40,279
I think she did it
only to humiliate Ms. Claire

563
00:48:40,280 --> 00:48:42,480
and let the press know the truth.

564
00:48:45,320 --> 00:48:47,040
But I'm worried about one thing.

565
00:48:48,520 --> 00:48:50,400
She won't tell her the truth, right?

566
00:48:56,040 --> 00:48:57,560
Are you doing okay?

567
00:49:19,440 --> 00:49:21,559
- What are you doing?
- Cha.

568
00:49:21,560 --> 00:49:24,839
We're here to see
the architectural drawings.

569
00:49:24,840 --> 00:49:26,800
<i>Open it then. I'd love to see them too.</i>

570
00:49:28,520 --> 00:49:30,679
<i>Chris, do you think
the Claire we see walking around</i>

571
00:49:30,680 --> 00:49:32,239
<i>is the real deal?</i>

572
00:49:32,240 --> 00:49:34,759
Do you think Ms. Cha told
Grandpa about the vault?

573
00:49:34,760 --> 00:49:36,039
<i>You're still up, Grandpa.</i>

574
00:49:36,040 --> 00:49:37,799
<i>Let me talk to Chan for a bit.</i>

575
00:49:37,800 --> 00:49:39,239
<i>Please don't hurt Ms. Wan.</i>

576
00:49:39,240 --> 00:49:41,079
I have no intention of hurting her.

577
00:49:41,080 --> 00:49:43,640
I was referring to the woman named Jinla.
